            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life and Education</strong><br>\nSusan B. Anthony was born in 1820 into a Quaker family with a strong sense of justice. From a young age, she was taught that everyone was equal under God, which fueled her later activism. She began teaching at the age of 17 to help her family during financial hardships.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Temperance Movement</strong><br>\nAnthony's activism began with the temperance movement, advocating for the prohibition of alcohol, believing it led to many social problems. However, her inability to speak at temperance events because she was a woman led her to pursue women's rights.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Women's Suffrage Movement</strong><br>\nSusan B. Anthony is most renowned for her work in the women's suffrage movement. She campaigned tirelessly for women's right to vote and even illegally voted in the 1872 Presidential election, leading to her arrest and trial.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
